WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.099 --> 00:00:15.609
Viruses, they really want to take over a cell
because interestingly viruses don't have all

00:00:15.609 --> 00:00:19.000
of the things
that they need to make copies of themselves.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:25.110
And, like everything on this planet in order
to continue being present on this planet

00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:27.340
we all have to make a copy of ourselves, right?

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:33.780
And that's why people have children,
that's why pets have babies,

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:39.039
that's why bacteria will divide,
and you know-- expand their population.

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:42.699
Viruses also need to do that or else they
won't exist anymore, right?

00:00:42.699 --> 00:00:48.760
And so viruses actually will use the things
that we have already inside of our cells.

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:57.780
So, our cells have all these amazing machines,
like proteins and other things that can make

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:00.079
different copies of cell pieces.

00:01:00.079 --> 00:01:06.130
And, so viruses come into our cells,
and they basically like hijack all of that

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:08.480
stuff,
so that it'll take over our cells,

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:14.869
so that we can make copies of their pieces,
so that they can continue making sure there's

00:01:14.869 --> 00:01:18.530
always more viruses being made.

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:24.090
And, so when that happens to our cells in
a way that really hurts

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:28.899
our cells we end up having an immune response.

00:01:28.899 --> 00:01:33.039
Sometimes our immune response just gets rid
of the virus right away,

00:01:33.039 --> 00:01:37.219
and sometimes we need a little extra help
from meds.

00:01:37.219 --> 00:01:40.299
And, so that's why viruses get us sick.

